# tests/chat-tools, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST. The subject is llm-step's INLINE FILE TOOLS — what the worker
# does with a queued batch of write/read/edit/ls calls — and the client was
# here to type `chat`, which is a different subject with a test of its own.
# So this drives llm-step the way the client does: mint the human turn, publish
# the admission event, dispatch, and read the turn commit back.
#
# dev/worker-test, not std/bash: reading and writing the conversation REF is the
# one thing caos gives a worker no verb for, so this needs git — and nothing
# else the client was providing.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/worker-test --worker1:@=worker.sh --bash:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --llm-step:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-step --stub:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-stub --common:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test/worker-common.sh
